# Belt and braces. These files already live OUTSIDE the document root, so no
# request should ever reach this directory — the only way out is
# /support/attachment/{id}, which checks who is asking first.
#
# This file exists for the deployment where somebody points a vhost at the
# project root instead of public/, which is a common shared-hosting mistake and
# would otherwise expose every bank screenshot on the platform at a guessable
# path. Denying here costs nothing and removes that class of accident.
Require all denied
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
  Order allow,deny
  Deny from all
</IfModule>
